  "name": "Color-GF(3)-Tiling: Hyperbolic Chromatic Diffusion",
  "theory": "causal-loop",
  "notebook": {
    "cellContents": {
      "c0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "c0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
        "content": "# Color x GF(3) x Tiling x Hyperbolicity\n\nThe chromatic diffusion framework where:\n- Colors live in GF(3) = {-1, 0, +1} with conservation law sum -> 0\n- Tilings provide the graph structure (dual graph: tiles=nodes, shared edges=adjacency)\n- Hyperbolicity of the tiling graph controls mixing rate via Cheeger -> spectral gap -> O(log n)\n- The Potts model on the tiling gives the coloring distribution; Glauber dynamics gives the Markov chain\n\n## Rigor Levels (Tao framework)\n- **Pre-rigorous**: Run experiments on small tilings, show convergence plots\n- **Rigorous**: Prove spectral gap via Chen-Liu-Vigoda spectral independence\n- **Post-rigorous**: Understand WHY via Gromov quasi-isometry to tree factor\n\n## Key Bounds\n- q=3 colors, Delta=max degree of tiling graph\n- Dobrushin regime: q > 2*Delta (restrictive for q=3)\n- Spectral independence: q >= 1.809*Delta (flip dynamics)\n- Hyperbolic tilings: spectral gap >= const > 0 (Cheeger positive)\n- Tree content: O(log m) mixing (0-hyperbolic)"
      },
